This is a step-by-step AWS Lambda Docker deployment setup using AWS CLI. It shows how to configure AWS CLI, verify the installation, build a Docker image for a Lambda container, and create an Amazon ECR repository.

Here it is as shown in your images:

===

AWS CLI - Download and Install it

https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/getting-started-install.html

Step1: Write Lambda Handler functions and respective functions
Step2: Open Visual Studio and locate to this folder
Step3: Create Docker file
Step4:open terminal in Visual Studio
and past this command
before that check aws was configured
aws --configure
        Enter:

        • Access Key ID

        • Secret Access Key

        • Region: ap-south-1

        • Output: json

After installation check this
aws --version
Should get like this
aws-cli/2.15.3 Python/3.11.5 Windows/10 exe/AMD64 prompt/off

Then issue this command

$env:DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0

docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t rag-lambda-containerhope .

aws ecr create-repository --repository-name rag-lambda-
container-hope --region ap-south-1

